@@ -10,6 +10,20 @@ Prints chosen columns of a CSV file, picked by their header names.
 
 The header row is printed first, then the chosen columns of every row, joined with the delimiter.
 
+## Supported input
+
+csvcut splits each line on the delimiter. It is not a full CSV parser: quotes get no special
+treatment.
+
+| Feature                                  | Supported | Notes                                   |
+|------------------------------------------|-----------|-----------------------------------------|
+| Select columns by header name            | yes       | `-f name,email`, in the order given     |
+| Select columns by position (`-f 2`)      | no        | `-f` takes header names only            |
+| A delimiter other than a comma (`-d`)    | yes       | `-d ';'`, also used to join the output  |
+| Quoted fields that contain the delimiter | no        | `"Smith, J"` is split into two fields   |
+| Quoted fields that contain a line break  | no        | Each line is read as its own row        |
+| Windows (CRLF) line endings              | yes       | The `\r` is dropped with the line break |
+
 ## Tests
 
     make test
